course: dictionary
lesson: 5552
title: Lemon: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lemon is an oval yellow fruit with sour juice. «Lick a lemon and it is sour» tells you how it tastes. But lemon can also be a word for a taste, a colour, or a thing that does not work well, so read the words around it to find out which meaning is right.
explain: «Mum said the old car was a real lemon.» Cars do not grow on trees, and they are not yellow fruit. The clue is «does not work properly», so here a lemon means something that keeps breaking down. Always ask: what word would fit here?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «a slice of lemon» becomes «a slice of a broken car», the sentence no longer makes sense, so you know lemon means the fruit here. When the meaning fits, you have found the right one.
fact: A lemon is an oval yellow fruit with sour juice and thick peel.
fact: Lemon can also mean the taste or colour of this fruit, as in «lemon cake» or «lemon yellow».
fact: Informally, a lemon is something, often a car, that does not work properly.
fact: Lemon juice is an acid, so it can turn red cabbage indicator pink in a science lesson.
fact: «When life gives you lemons, make lemonade» means make the best of a bad situation.
exercise: «Lick a lemon and it is sour; taste a tiny pinch of baking soda and it is bitter and soapy.» In this sentence, what is a lemon? | A car that does not work properly | A sweet pudding | *An oval yellow fruit with sour juice | A kind of baking soda
exercise: Mum says, «Our old car is a real lemon.» What does lemon mean here? | A sour yellow fruit | *Something that does not work properly | A lemonade stall | A pale yellow colour
exercise: In «lemon yellow», what does lemon describe? | *The colour | The taste | A fruit tree | A broken car
test: «Suck a slice of lemon and your whole face screws up.» Which meaning of lemon fits? | *The sour fruit | A car that breaks down | A yellow dress | A glass of lemonade with ice
test: Which phrase means make the best of a bad situation? | *When life gives you lemons, make lemonade | Lemon juice brings the purple back | A slice of lemon | Squeeze a lemon
exam: Which sentence uses lemon as an adjective? | *«The cake was lemon-flavoured.» | «Squeeze a lemon over the fish.» | «Lick a lemon and it is sour.» | «He bought a lemon from the garage.»
